---
import ToolLayout from '../../layouts/ToolLayout.astro';
import CronTool from '../../components/CronTool.jsx';
---
<ToolLayout title="Cron Expression Builder & Explainer" description="Build a cron expression from presets, or paste one to get a plain-English explanation of what it means.">
  <CronTool client:load slot="tool" />
  <h2>Reading cron syntax</h2>
  <p>A cron expression has 5 fields — minute, hour, day of month, month, and day of week — each controlling when a scheduled job runs. Getting the field order wrong is a common source of "why didn't my job run" bugs.</p>

  <h2>Common mistakes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Mixing up field order</strong>, especially confusing minute/hour position with day/month position.</li>
    <li><strong>Not realizing day-of-month and day-of-week are OR'd together</strong> in most cron implementations, not AND'd as many people expect.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Use cases</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Building a cron schedule for a new scheduled job</li>
    <li>Understanding what an existing cron expression from documentation actually means</li>
    <li>Debugging why a scheduled job ran at an unexpected time</li>
  </ul>
</ToolLayout>
